    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Explain what $f'(3)=5$ means for a tangent to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=3$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The tangent at $(3,f(3))$ has gradient $5$.",
      "worked": "By definition, $f'(3)$ is the gradient of the tangent to $y=f(x)$ at $x=3$. Hence the tangent at $(3,f(3))$ has gradient $5$.",
